+## Why
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document rather than the whole new version. The library can apply a JSON Patch but cannot produce one.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returning an RFC 6902 JSON Patch that turns `from` into `to` when passed to `applyPatch`.
+- The patch is minimal in extent: it recurses into objects and arrays and describes only the places that differ; equal documents give `[]`.
+- Array item insertion/removal yields a single `add`/`remove` for that item; a moved item yields a `move` or a `remove` + `add`, never rewrites of the items around it.
+- Neither input is mutated and the patch shares no structure with them.
+- Not breaking: purely additive; no existing export changes.
+
+Governing standards: RFC 6902 (JSON Patch, §4 operations, §4.6 equality) and RFC 6901 (JSON Pointer, §3 and §4 escaping of `~` and `/`).
+
+Out of scope: guaranteeing the globally shortest patch (e.g. detecting every `copy`), `test` operations, validating that inputs are JSON, a CLI/URI-fragment form.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch-creation`: producing a minimal RFC 6902 patch from two JSON documents.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: new exported function and helpers (reuses existing `clone`, `jsonEqual`, `isObject`).
+- Tests in `test/`; README gains a short section. No dependencies added.
